It is my first time behind the counter.
The café is not open yet.
One of the experienced volunteers calls for me.
We stand in front of the large espresso machine.
"Today you must learn to make coffee," he says.
I have never made coffee on such a machine before.
The first step is to grind the coffee beans.
He presses a small button.
The machine grinds the brown beans with a loud sound.
The second step is to steam the milk.
He pours cold milk into a metal jug.
Afterwards he turns on the hot steam.
I look closely at his hands meanwhile.
The milk in the jug quickly becomes warm and thick.
He has clearly made coffee many times before.
When I arrived this morning, I was very nervous.
But he explained it well, so I have already understood most of it.
